Cycle counters specification

Regardless whether the cell is new or not the cell cycle counters shall be set to 0 for the first time.
The counters can remain to 0 until a capacity estimation is made for each cell. 
The cycles counters shall keep track of the consumed cycles.

Cycle count = Total Ah throughput / 2.Cnom.
Note: Cnom must be updated according to the new measurement capacity.

The cell manufacturer provides a table mapping the number of expected cycles vs the cell capacity retention.
Once the cell capacity has been estimated one can read the remaining cycles from this table and correct the cycle counter.

